#passage(("I don't agree with this term, our land or his land or my land. I think that as long as you're living in a place and I didn't kick you out of your own home, me taking the rulership of a place is not me taking your land. Because the Muslims were being persecuted in the lands that you're referring to. I'm here as a Muslim defending Islam. So when Islam went there, it was because the people were being persecuted in those lands. They were trying to help the people who were being persecuted in this land: first, hear the message of Truth; two, prevent the persecution that was happening to them, by the morals of Islam. The Muslims didn't go and say: OK, this is your house. Don't go outside. It's my house now! Muslims didn't do that.", "Ethnically cleansing means that you remove the ethnicity from land. You cleanse the land from the ethnicity. I would need to ask you for references for what you're talking about, because I don't agree that this took place. There's no ever ethnic cleansing that took place. If it did, there would be no Kurdish or [Turkish]. I agree that Muslims entered there and they ruled. I don't disagree with that. But you claiming that what they were doing is that they were saying, for example, leave the country because you are Turkish or you're Kurdish, you would have to give me evidence for that. Can you name me one academic historian, reliable one, which claimed that Muslims were doing this? If you claim Muslims are doing this, you have to give me at least one historian saying that. What I would advise you to do is go read the history, not from Muslims (you don't have to read it from Muslims); read it from people who aren't biased towards any religion, they're just giving you historical point of view.", "The Ottoman Empire, in which actually Muslims were one structure, where there was a Caliphate, a leader of the Muslims, that died way before what you're talking about. So if you want to put the responsibility on that, as I said, I separate between the people and the religion. If it was a Muslim Caliphate, then maybe I might look at the claim. But still, I separate between what they do, unless it was justified by the Scripture. I cannot blame Islam based on what someone did wrong. He did a genocide, the Armenian genocide; I'm not justifying anything which happened which is un-Islamic by a Muslim.", "You have to be objective. You cannot base your feelings just because someone misused something which is True. You cannot push away something which is True, instead of blaming the person who is doing wrong. What you should do is to blame the individual who is doing wrong. There are so many Muslims that didn't do what you're talking about. If just a group of Muslims did it, then you cannot blame everyone and the religion. It has to be rationality.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Ex-Muslims Question Islam P2! Muhammed Ali - Speakers Corner”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AXViHAPPte0", ((382, "6:22–7:36"), (475, "7:55–9:28"), (617, "10:17–10:54"), (660, "11:00–11:20"),), id: 3119)
