#passage(("The first 24-hour hospital in Baghdad: treatment wasn't only 24 hours, but it was free, for everyone! Now, even in this day and age today, the people who want to talk to us like they are coming from a moral high ground and enlightenment period, they don't have this idea of treating you for free. You have to pay in most places. And if there is free health service in many countries, it's the worst service that you could possibly have. This was the peak of civilisation, and peak of medicine, and it was for free, and it was for everyone, anyone who was sick. Then we have the first university.", "A lot of the Westerners have no clue that this was the Islamic history that was going on. And the reality, the civilisation that we're living in today is heavily, if not 90% of it, built upon this Islamic foundation. Now, of course, we're not going to take the credit from the scientists and the intelligent people within the Western world who used this information and developed it and enhanced it in many ways. That is for sure the case. You take previous knowledge and you build upon it, but you don't take away the foundation! You don't show ingratitude to the people who allowed you to reach where you are today.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| Responding To Professor Jiang's Lecture On The Islamic Golden Age | Muhammed Ali!”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6SVGKQ-xiGs", ((1771, "29:31–30:34"), (1838, "30:38–31:10"),), id: 3124)
