#passage(("Most of the things that are advancements today in science are based in origin of Muslim inventions. For example, Algorithms that you use comes from a Muslim mathematician, he was called Al-Khawarizmy. Al-Khawarizmy literally is the translation of Algorithm. This is where the word literally comes from, because he's the one who invented this idea of Algorithms. These things I'm saying are not hidden secrets; you can just Google this information and you will see what I'm telling you.", "Islam and science, they go hand in hand, but Islam understands that science is an instrument and it can be right and wrong. It doesn't lead you to absolute truth, while Revelation from God is absolute Truth. So if something which is not absolute opposes something which is absolute, of course we would reject that which is not absolute.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Why Does God Not Communicate With Humans? Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1c92faSXNec", ((848, "14:08–14:36"), (882, "14:42–14:53"),), id: 3126)
