#passage(("AlHassan ibn alHaytham, the world's first true scientist. This is a huge thing to mention for those people, especially today in the West, who are fascinated with science; they don't understand. He's the first person to develop the MODERN METHOD, this idea of experimentation, repeatability and falsification, and you can say the inventor of camera, these two ideas in his book, Optics. And he says that it influenced the Renaissance, from 14th to the 17th century, where Europe actually was revived and it started using that knowledge. But nobody talks about where this knowledge came from, where they revived from this Dark Ages into the ages that they became later on.", "So the reality is this knowledge is all exported, taken away from the Muslims, people like these individuals. He didn't mention many people, like for example 'Abbas bin Firnas; he was the first human being to fly in human history. So many people, some of the names that he's mentioned and many, many more, that are not highlighted in Western history for a reason, and I mentioned that reason.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| Responding To Professor Jiang's Lecture On The Islamic Golden Age | Muhammed Ali!”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6SVGKQ-xiGs", ((1676, "27:56–28:35"), (1720, "28:40–29:00"),), id: 3128)
