#passage(("You need to realize one thing. The Quran is a text that comes 1,400 years ago. The verse that says the clouds are heavy comes 1,400 years ago. 1,400 years ago, the Muslims started in the deserts of Arabia: camel [herding], no advancements, no science. Now, this is a confusion that a lot of people make. When you talk about advancements of Muslims and science, which was mainly in [Andalusia] in Spain, we're talking about 700 years ago, not 1,400 years ago. So when I bring you a verse from the Quran that says that the clouds are heavy, this is 1,400 years ago. So you cannot say: \"Oh, they studied it.\" Your argument is false, because they were not studying anything that time. The reason these people advanced was because of the Quran, because the Quran teaches you to seek knowledge, walk in the earth and learn and study. So the reason we advanced, as you say we advance, is because we followed the book. We use the book as a principle to look at the world and study and learn.", "Now you said we stopped. Yes. Because every empire has a stopping point. No empire lasts forever. So you have the Ottoman Empire, hundreds of years lasting. America is a baby empire, not even 100 years. So empires rise and fall. When Muslims were in power, of course, there was more advancing and learning. When Muslims were defeated by Europeans, you know what they did? They went into our libraries. They took the knowledge and they burnt our books. So it's not like they were learning and then they stopped learning. No, historically they were attacked. Their knowledge were taken, adopted, applied in the west, and then they burnt our libraries. They burnt our books. So there is a reason for this knowledge stopping, because of what happened historically.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Buddhist Gets Defensive After A Muslim Highlights The Problems With Buddhism! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cCyN0gL4kEI", ((3267, "54:27–56:41"), (3404, "56:44–57:31"),), id: 3130)
