#passage(("He essentially put the picture of what we refer to as \"the Dome of the Rock\", قُبَّة الصَّخرة (Qubbat asSakhra), and he called the Qubbat asSakhra, or the Dome of the Rock, as alAqsa Mosque. That's not accurate, and that's a very ABC kind of mistake. That's like elementary school, when it comes to history. If you just did a bit of research and googling, you would know that this is incorrect. The Masjid Qubbat asSakhra, this mosque of the Dome of the Rock, is not what we call Al Masjid alAqsa. It's not what Muslims believe to be the Masjid alAqsa. So perhaps you have a mystery there because you are conflating terms and ideas and understanding.", "AlMasjid alAqsa is this entire space that you see that is fenced, which is like 144,000 square meters, and it has a lot of different historical monuments or historical things within, over a hundred things that are there that are historical. And this entire fenced area is what we refer to as alMasjid alAqsa. There's even a مُصَلَّى (Musalla: which is a place to pray) there, which people also refer to as AlMasjid alAqsa, which is the Masjid alQibla, the Masjid alQibli, the mosque of the Qibla, and it was called that because it's in the direction of the Qibla. And we don't say that alone also is alMasjid alAqsa. AlMasjid alAqsa, like I said, is the entire space. So it's not like Muslims have built alMasjid alAqsa over the Temple Mount. That's not accurate.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| Responding To Professor Jiang's Lecture On The Islamic Golden Age | Muhammed Ali!”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6SVGKQ-xiGs", ((645, "10:45–11:16"), (686, "11:26–12:09"),), id: 3136)
