#passage(("The reason I chose to speak about the beliefs of a Muslim is because there will be a day that will come, sooner or later, where there will be a fight between the Muslims and the non-muslims. Today they are slaughtering our brothers and sisters, they are slaughtering children, they're slaughtering women, tens of thousands, and there's nothing happening to them. And they're fighting against a very small group, and they're still being defeated by that very small group. But in reality there is no equal fighting: there's no other state, there's no Army, there's no weapons against them, there's no Muslims fighting them. But is the time going to come where Muslims are going to fight against specifically [Bani Israel]? Of course it's going to come; there's no doubt about that. This is a reality.", "So the time will come. The question is: when the time comes, when you look at Muslims today, I want you to actually be sincere with yourself, sit down and say: okay, our Muslims today, the way we are as [an ummah] today, the Tik Tok [ummah] and the lgbtq [ummah], is ready for this? Are we ready when the time comes? So how can we be ready? What separated us from the previous generations is what they believed, is their [iman], what they held in their hearts, deep in their hearts. That is what separated them from us. That is what made them have the victory that they had.", "Now, when the time comes, we need to be prepared. Allah says in the Quran: \"[And] prepare for them.\" Who's them? All disbelievers equally; doesn't matter who they are. What is Allah asking us to prepare? Strength. Now, many said strength here is not referring to military power, is not referring to weaponry. Why? Because Allah in the next verse says \"and from horses\", and horses is military power; it's weapons. If you have guns today, they was horses that time. So Allah is saying first: this strength that we have to prepare, other than the military weapons, is the strength of [iman], the strength of