#passage(("The problems that we encounter as Muslims in this Duniya (Worldly life) are two types of فِتن (Fitan: Trials). Fitna in the Arabic language means a trial and tribulation. We have the Fitna of Shubuhat (Shubuhat: Suspicions) and the Fitna of Shahawat (Shahawat: Lusts). The Fitna of Shubuhat is the fitna of doubt: when you encounter a doubt, a problem, something problematic that you do not know how to answer. People talk to you about Islam with some questions that you're not familiar with. So this is the first thing, the Fitna of Doubts, Shubuhat: the people teach you deviancy, they give you misguidance. And the second type is Shahawat, Desires. All humans have desires: men have desires, women have desires, Muslims have desires, and these desires lead them to do what? Sins! So the other type of problem is sins: someone drinking Alcohol, someone committing Zina (Fornication), someone doesn't pray. And which one is actually more severe? For Muslims, it is the Fitna of Shubuhat!",), "The Muslim Lantern, “The Situation Of The Ummah, The Disease & The Cure | Al Muwahiddeen Mosque - The Netherlands |”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0ycNKKOx2jg", ((110, "1:50–2:54"),), id: 3139)
