#passage(("I don't think that it necessarily is based on race. I think it's more based on an economic situation of the individual. If they look at you as a rich person, they're not going to treat you as a [second-class] citizen if you come to the country as a billionaire or millionaire. But they exploit the fact that these people are poor right now. Now with Sudan, I'm not a political commentator. I don't do this research into the events that take place. However, from what I've heard, there are countries that are getting involved in Sudan in a negative way, in an evil way, for their own benefit and their own resources, and that's absolutely to be condemned, and it's absolutely against Islam. These people are murderous and these people are criminals. Now, however, if someone presents me that exact details and proof, I'm more than happy to accept. I'm talking about what I heard, what I know.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Inquisitive Agnostic Grills Muslim On Cousin Marriage And Racism In Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fvVrT_WHQxg", ((916, "15:16–16:14"),), id: 3145)
