#passage(("When you say \"why is this country not helping?\", my point is, to single out a specific country is inconsistent. I believe every Muslim country has a responsibility there, because if one country does not act, then the responsibility moves to the other Muslim Country. If that other country doesn't act, then it moves to the other country. Why are they not acting? I share the same sentiment, more than you do even. To think that governments that are in Muslim Lands, they're not being influenced by Zionists, is naive. I believe that it is very difficult, if not impossible, for someone to become a president in a country without already being approved by certain individuals. No one can be just a Muslim Leader in a Muslim Country without already being \"approved\" by certain individuals. Why? Because Zionists know very well, if there are good leaders, or correct leaders, or if Muslims unite around them, they're not going to have safety! How are they going to have safety if the countries around them can attack them any day?",), "The Muslim Lantern, “IDF Soldier Confronted A Muslim Live Then THIS HAPPENED! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-qnYJXIxSpc", ((392, "6:32–7:49"),), id: 3147)
