#refbox("Reference text: Quran 5:79, quran.com (Saheeh International)", (("5:79", "They used not to prevent one another from wrongdoing that they did. How wretched was that which they were doing."),))
// U ML041:562-647 | The Muslim Lantern | 4
#passage(("You have people who are failing the test and you have people who are succeeding the test. Allah said that you command good and you forbid evil, and you believe in God. Without these two things, we're not the best people. Can't be the best. And best people doesn't mean race. Doesn't mean any of that. 80% of Muslims are non-Arabs. We're talking about Islam, Muslims. It's not race or any of that.", "There are people living comfortably. If I'm living comfortably, sitting in my house, I'm enjoying my tea, I'm enjoying my drink. Who cares? This kid is losing his limbs. I couldn't care less. He can't see with his eyes. I couldn't care. I'm eating. I'm drinking. This is the crazy world that we live in today. We need to make them realize, maybe they will care about this little more, if you make them realize the impact is going to come to you whether you like it or not. When, for instance, the Strait of Hormuz is closed, prices are going up here as well. When you're bombing countries in the Middle East or any other place, you start having immigrants coming here and then you complain about immigrants. This is one way I use with them: \"You got to realize it's going to come to you. Don't ignore. The effect is going to come to you. It's going to come to your family. It's going to come to everyone in the end.\" So, if you pretend and act as if you don't care about evil happening in the world, you're going to be influenced in the end by that evil yourself.", "It's like beating a dead horse in English. They also have examples like that in Arabic: \"There is no life in the one you're calling.\" You can call but there is no life there. But there's always someone watching and you don't know. This is our attitude that we need to take. God is the one who guides. There are people who are enemies of Islam. There's this guy in the Netherlands or somewhere. He was a part of the parliament actually and he was against Muslims, speaking against them. He wrote a book. And he accepted Islam. He was a hater of Islam and he accepted it. So, you never know. Maybe the biggest hater becomes the [supporter], because he studied, he realized that this must be from God.", "That's the impact I'm saying: 0.0001. If you also said, \"You know what? Everything is destructed, everything is gone. So, I'm going to just ignore everything,\" that person would have continued being the person they are. We got to do as much as we can.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Curious Couple Ask A Muslim To Explain World Suffering! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9AACeXB0A9Q", ((1512, "25:12–25:39"), (1549, "25:49–26:48"), (1613, "26:53–27:41"), (1689, "28:09–28:26"),), id: 3158)
// U ML025:368-435 | The Muslim Lantern | 5
#passage(("If I talk about Sudan, there's many Muslims that talk about this, including myself. It's not only Sudan, obviously. There's many other countries that also been wrongdoing. And we talk about these issues. So, when it comes to talking, we talk.", "There's a few things there. The first thing is, for instance, the idea that the people are overworking people, they're not paying them enough money for the work that they do. Someone can easily come back and say they are choosing to do this. Nobody's forcing them to do this. \"We're agreeing with them to pay them this amount and they're accepting it. They're consenting that we are going to accept this specific amount of money in exchange for this specific amount of work. Any day if they wanted to go back to their country, the border is open. They can take a plane and they can return to their countries.\" Someone say, \"What are you protesting about?\" They can make the argument very easily.", "Now the second thing you say, about Muslims stopping something: [the Prophet] told us that whoever sees of you an evil thing or a bad thing, or something that needs to be corrected, let him stop it with his hand. \"If he cannot\": so here he shows us that not every situation we can get involved, as you said, boots on the ground. If he cannot, then with his tongue. If he cannot even speak with his tongue, let him hate it with his heart, and that is the weakest of faith. The weakest of faith is just like you can't do anything, you just hate it with your heart, but you at least have to hate it with your heart or you have no faith at all. You have to hate the evil that is happening in your heart at the very least.", "So when you say boots on the ground, we have issues with that, because that can cause more harm than it can cause good, if we say to the people, \"Get on the ground, fight the governments,\" have people being killed. We've seen many revolutions happen. They call the Arab Spring, and then you look at the situation of the countries. Sudan is one of the examples. A revolution happened, boots on the ground, and look at the situation now: is worse than it was before. You look at Egypt, is the same story. Look at almost every country that had Arab Spring, which is mostly being controlled by the West so they can make a revolution or whatever. In the end, when the ruler is removed, the west puts in a worse ruler than the one who was there before. The economy of the country gets destroyed. [Libya] is an example. Look at the Arab Muslim world and you'll see this.", "So we say that if we want to do something, the purpose is to change. If what I'm going to do is not going to change it, it's going to create a greater harm, then no, I shouldn't be doing that, because it's going to be a greater harm to destabilize a country, have armies fighting people and hundreds of thousands or tens of thousands of people killed. That is worse than the state that it was already in. So if you want to do something, you got to make sure that this thing is going to fix the issue. It's going to change the situation. It's not going to lead to a worse situation than the one it was in already.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Inquisitive Agnostic Grills Muslim On Cousin Marriage And Racism In Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fvVrT_WHQxg", ((1249, "20:49–21:03"), (1306, "21:46–22:20"), (1349, "22:29–23:04"), (1384, "23:04–23:53"), (1433, "23:53–24:29"),), id: 3159)
